Go 1.21+ strips DWARF symbols even with `-ldflags="-s -w"`, forcing Ghidra to rely on heuristic decompilation. The Go ABI 0x1 uses an internal register-passing convention: parameters ≤16 bytes are passed via registers (R8–R15), larger parameters via stack. Ghidra plugins (`go-reko`, `ghidra-go-tool`) parse the `.gopclntab` section which contains PC-to-line mappings and `funcID` entries. For an exported function `NewServer(addr string, port int) *Server`, Ghidra decompiles:
```go
undefined8 NewServer(char *addr,undefined8 port,int param_3)
{
  iVar1 = strcmp(addr,"127.0.0.1");
  if (iVar1 == 0) {
