```
The analyst must manually annotate ESP-relative stack frames because Ghidra’s AABI rules mis-align Go’s dedicated register window (DX, AX, CX, BX, SP, BP, SI, DI via R8–R15 aliases). Real-world: The APT41 campaign (2024-Q2) used stripped Go 1.21 binaries to exfiltrate victim data via DNS tunnelling; analysts reconstructed exported functions via `objdump -g` on the `.gopclntab` section and cross-validated against Go’s `runtime` source.

